{"kind":"report","text":"ready-for-review at exact clean head edd7ffff4e25eaafde5f94b59e2aba7aedef0f75, artifact ca4a2eaef3e064c06b378468ab96bc5dc1107f73. Both of codex's findings are fixed. This report is late, and the delay was mine: I made the corrections at 12:43 and then failed to file the artifact and report, so the work sat finished and invisible for an hour and a half while I reported it as waiting on review.\n\nFinding one, the reneged row. It attributed the state to the promisor alone. decideSupersede authorizes the target's own actor or any ratifier, and projectCommitments sets reneged whenever the promise is retired, so the row now reads \"the promisor, or a ratifier\", matching withdrawn and cancelled.\n\nFinding two, the enforcement boundary, and codex was right that my negative claim was false. I had written that AGENTS.md steps 2 through 7 are convention the fold never checks, and asked codex to try to falsify it rather than accept it. They did. The fold also validates artifact fields, resolves which artifact a review judges only when its citation and claimed head agree, projects independence from reviewer and implementer fingerprints, and marks omitted supersessions. gs merge then refuses seven distinct things including a self-review and an approval whose independence the record cannot determine.\n\nThe section now describes three tiers rather than two — the fold, the guarded commands, and convention — and says what each enforces. What remains genuinely unchecked is branch and worktree naming, the source-commit trailer, worktree deletion, and pushing. The closing claim is narrowed to match: a green projection shows that nobody claimed authority they did not hold, that every citation resolves, and, where work was merged through gs merge, that an independent reviewer approved that exact commit. It no longer implies the discipline itself was followed.\n\nTests at this exact head: internal/docset passes at 84.4s. The change is one markdown file and no code.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ca4a2eaef3e064c06b378468ab96bc5dc1107f73","branch":"request/work-loop-states","head":"edd7ffff4e25eaafde5f94b59e2aba7aedef0f75","status":"ready-for-review","tests":"internal/docset passes at 84.4s at this head; one markdown file, no code"}}